      "key": "withdrawal",
      "name": "Host silent",
      "expected": "Nothing from the MAC-move host reaches either MLAG peer. After the 10 s ageing time both peers remove the host MAC from the bridge host table: CHR 1 its entry on ether5, CHR 2 its entry on the peer port ether2. Frames to the host MAC are then unknown unicast, so both peers flood streams 101 and 102 to the other traffic host as well. This is correct bridge behaviour and is recorded, not failed. Every stream to or from the host loses probes for the whole silence; that loss is the fault itself, so the limit is the 25 s silence plus the 1 s relearn target. Stream 302 and both bypass streams lose nothing.",
